  "mechanismSummary": "A ring π bond attacks the sulfur of SO₃ as an S=O π pair moves onto oxygen. Hydrogen sulfate removes the ring proton, and the sulfuric acid formed protonates the sulfonate, giving benzenesulfonic acid and hydrogen sulfate back. Sulfonation is reversible: heating in dilute acid removes the SO₃H group again.",
